# Remora boot-property setup (bd remora-28ix.4).
#
# The host contract is androidboot.remora_*; init turns every androidboot.<key> on its own argv
# into ro.boot.<key>. Two of those need a second property set from them, and that is all this
# file does now.
#
# THIS WAS AN ADAPTER AND IS NOT ONE ANY MORE (bd remora-28ix.4 step 4). It used to
# map fourteen ro.boot.remora_* keys onto the inherited pre-migration names, for consumers that
# read that older namespace: the init triggers in the upstream vendor rc, and above all the
# closed composer prebuilt, which had no source in the tree and so could never be renamed. Every
# one of those consumers is gone — the upstream vendor and device projects left both manifests,
# Remora's own composer HAL replaced the prebuilt, gpu_config.sh and the three native modules
# read ro.boot.remora_* directly, and remora.common.rc fires its own remora_overlayfs trigger.
# A mapping onto names nothing reads is not compatibility, it is two properties for every one.
#
# WHAT REMAINS IS NOT MAPPING. Both stanzas below set a DIFFERENT property from the one they
# match on, which is why they were never part of the adapter's job and do not leave with it:
#   - lcd_density, because init matches all early-init actions against property state when the
#     event is dequeued, BEFORE any of their commands run. A setprop in one early-init action
#     therefore cannot arm another early-init property action, so this cannot be deferred to a
#     stanza keyed on ro.boot.remora_dpi elsewhere — it has to happen here, in the same action.
#   - ro.hardware.vulkan, which is a per-deploy fact rather than a per-image one: a build-time
#     pin is write-once and beat every runtime decision (bd remora-xqt1), so the ICD is a boot
#     arg and this is where it lands.
#
# ONE FILE, TWO DELIVERY ROADS, and it must stay byte-identical on both (test-enforced):
#   - bind-mounted to /vendor/etc/init/remora.props.rc by buildDockerRunArgv on every deploy,
#     the same road as remora-fwd.rc;
#   - installed at the same path by vendor/remora's own vendor.mk, so the image stands alone.
# Init parses the path once; when both roads deliver, the mount shadows the identical install.

on early-init && property:ro.boot.remora_dpi=*
    setprop ro.sf.lcd_density ${ro.boot.remora_dpi}

on early-init && property:ro.boot.remora_vulkan=*
    setprop ro.hardware.vulkan ${ro.boot.remora_vulkan}
